---
// The publication's identity page: what this is, what it is not, and where the figures come
// from. Exists for readers first, and second for the search and answer engines that need an
// entity to attach the work to. Plain register, no em-dashes, no self-congratulation.
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { ORG, DEFAULT_DESCRIPTION } from "../lib/seo.mjs";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About, Owner Scorecard"
  description={DEFAULT_DESCRIPTION}
  jsonLd={{
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "AboutPage",
    name: "About Owner Scorecard",
    mainEntity: ORG,
  }}
>
  <section class="about">
    <h1>About</h1>

    <p>
      Owner Scorecard is an independent research publication. It lays a business out the way an
      owner would read it: roughly a decade of revenue, margins, returns on capital, owner
      earnings, buybacks, share count, and debt, every figure traced to the company's own
      filings.
    </p>

    <p>
      The publication carries no ratings, price targets, or estimates.
    </p>

    <p>
      The figures come from primary sources: annual and quarterly reports filed with the SEC, and
      the equivalent filings for the Japan and ADR catalogs. Where a number is computed, the
      <a href="/concepts">Principles</a> page defines the computation. Where a company's own
      disclosure is thin, the page says so.
    </p>

    <p>
      Research Notes are published under the publication's name. Errors, once found, are
      corrected at the foot of the page, the note's updated date is changed to say so, and the
      change is logged in the public <a href="/corrections">corrections record</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Ownership and independence</h2>

    <p>
      Owner Scorecard is independently owned and is paid for by readers or by no one. Everything
      on the site today is free, and the record pages will stay free. There is no advertising,
      no sponsorship, and no broker referral; nothing in the publication's economics improves
      when a reader trades.
    </p>

    <p>
      The people who write here may own securities discussed on these pages. Positions may
      change, and no position is ever announced, not when it is opened and not when it is
      closed. Around any company the
      publication writes research on, personal trading stops five days before publication and
      does not resume until ten days after it. A dated log of every personal trade is kept. The
      reasoning behind these rules is set out in
      <a href="/notes/the-founding-letter">The Founding Letter</a>.
    </p>

    <p class="fine">
      Owner Scorecard is not registered as an investment adviser or broker-dealer. Nothing here
      is investment advice or a recommendation to buy or sell any security.
    </p>
  </section>

  <style>
    .about { max-width: 640px; }
    .about h1 { margin: 0 0 16px; }
    .about h2 { margin: 28px 0 12px; font-size: 1.2rem; }
    .about p { color: var(--ink-soft); }
    .fine { font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--muted); }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
